00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.360 align:start position:0%
shadow banking is worth more than 70  trillion dollars across the globe it  isn't just about risky investment  products and lending between individuals  shadow banking also covers loan shark  operations and pawn shops as well as  what are considered more respectable  activities like derivatives and  securities lending what makes them  shadowy is that they operate outside the  regular banking system and that means  it's often not controlled by regulators  the Financial Stability Board says  shadow banking poses systemic risks to  the global financial system the  prevalence of shadow banking makes it  difficult for governments of countries  like China and India to control their  economies through tools like interest  rates or money supply let's take a look  at China where shadow banking looms  largest it's estimated China's shadow  banking sector is worth 6 trillion  dollars about 69% of the economy that's  Vickers saving deposit rates in China  are low and most small businesses can't  get bank loans and so turn to other  sources of lending China tried to rein  in wealth management products last year  resulting in the worst cash crunch in  more than a decade Rosalyn chin  Bloomberg Hong Kong
 

